<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>AquaLens monitoring report · {{ location_label }}</title>
  <style>
    @page {
      size: A4;
      margin: 22mm 18mm;
      @bottom-center {
        content: "AquaLens · Page " counter(page) " of " counter(pages);
        font-family: "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
        font-size: 8pt;
        color: #6b7280;
      }
    }

    :root {
      --aqua: #0ea5b7;
      --aqua-dark: #0b6f7d;
      --ink: #0f172a;
      --mute: #475569;
      --line: #e2e8f0;
      --paper: #ffffff;
      --risk-low: #15803d;
      --risk-medium: #b45309;
      --risk-high: #b91c1c;
    }

    body {
      font-family: "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
      font-size: 10pt;
      color: var(--ink);
      line-height: 1.5;
      margin: 0;
    }

    h1, h2, h3 { color: var(--ink); }
    h1 { font-size: 22pt; margin: 0 0 4pt; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
    h2 { font-size: 14pt; margin: 18pt 0 8pt; }
    h3 { font-size: 11pt; margin: 12pt 0 4pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--mute); }

    .lede {
      font-size: 11pt;
      color: var(--mute);
      max-width: 540pt;
    }

    .header {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 22pt;
      border-bottom: 1pt solid var(--line);
      padding-bottom: 14pt;
      margin-bottom: 16pt;
    }

    .brand {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      flex: 0 0 auto;
    }

    /* Bundled AquaLens SVG embedded as a base64 data URL. The asset
       is 720 × 240 (3:1) and contains the glyph + wordmark + tagline +
       accent rule, so we just size the <img> and let it do the work. */
    .brand-image {
      width: 230pt;
      height: 77pt;
      display: block;
    }

    /* Fallback when the brand SVG fails to load — emitted by the
       template's brand_logo_data_url else branch below. */
    .brand-text {
      font-family: ui-monospace, "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
      font-size: 11pt;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      color: var(--aqua-dark);
      text-transform: lowercase;
    }

    .report-title {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
      min-width: 0;
      text-align: right;
    }

    .report-kicker-text {
      font-size: 10pt;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.16em;
      color: var(--aqua-dark);
      font-weight: 800;
      line-height: 1;
      margin: 0 0 4pt;
    }

    .report-title h1 {
      margin: 0 0 4pt;
      font-size: 20pt;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    .report-title .lede {
      font-size: 9.5pt;
      color: var(--mute);
      margin: 0;
    }

    .report-title .meta {
      margin-top: 8pt;
      font-size: 8.5pt;
      color: var(--mute);
      line-height: 1.45;
    }

    .report-title .meta .session-id {
      font-family: ui-monospace, "SFMono-Regular", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
      font-size: 7.8pt;
    }

    .risk-card {
      border: 1pt solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 10pt;
      padding: 14pt 16pt;
      margin: 14pt 0;
      background: #f8fafc;
    }

    /* Land / mixed-AOI warning banner. Sits above the risk card so the
       reader can't mistake a ground reflectance read for a water-quality
       assessment. */
    .aoi-banner {
      border: 1pt solid;
      border-radius: 8pt;
      padding: 10pt 14pt;
      margin: 4pt 0 16pt;
      page-break-inside: avoid;
      break-inside: avoid;
    }
    .aoi-banner-land {
      border-color: #fecaca;
      background: #fef2f2;
      color: #7f1d1d;
    }
    .aoi-banner-mixed {
      border-color: #fde68a;
      background: #fffbeb;
      color: #92400e;
    }
    .aoi-banner-title {
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 10pt;
      margin-bottom: 4pt;
    }
    .aoi-banner-body {
      font-size: 9pt;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }
    .aoi-banner-fraction {
      font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
      font-size: 8pt;
      opacity: 0.85;
    }

    .risk-grid {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      table-layout: fixed;
      margin-bottom: 6pt;
    }
    .risk-grid td {
      border: 0 !important;
      padding: 0 16pt 0 0 !important;
      vertical-align: middle;
    }
    .risk-grid td:last-child { padding-right: 0 !important; }
    .risk-grid .pill-cell { width: 100pt; }
    .risk-grid .score-cell { width: 128pt; }
    .risk-grid .urgency-cell { width: 120pt; }

    .risk-pill {
      display: inline-block;
      width: 92pt;
      padding: 5pt 0;
      border-radius: 999pt;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 11pt;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--paper);
      line-height: 1.15;
      text-align: center;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .risk-pill.low { background: var(--risk-low); }
    .risk-pill.medium { background: var(--risk-medium); }
    .risk-pill.high { background: var(--risk-high); }

    .risk-score {
      display: inline-block;
      line-height: 1.2;
      white-space: nowrap;
      font-size: 12pt;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--ink);
      letter-spacing: 0;
      margin-top: 1pt;
    }

    .risk-meta {
      display: block;
    }
    .risk-meta-label {
      font-size: 8pt;
      color: var(--mute);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 2pt;
    }
    .risk-meta-value {
      font-size: 11pt;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-transform: capitalize;
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    .urgency {
      font-size: 9pt;
      color: var(--mute);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    }

    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      font-size: 9.5pt;
    }
    /* Keep a label and its value together on the same page — critical for
       the glossary where a term cell and its description were getting split. */
    tr {
      page-break-inside: avoid;
      break-inside: avoid;
    }
    th, td {
      text-align: left;
      padding: 6pt 8pt;
      border-bottom: 1pt solid var(--line);
      vertical-align: top;
      page-break-inside: avoid;
      break-inside: avoid;
    }
    th { color: var(--mute); font-weight: 600; font-size: 8.5pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
    /* Each section should try to start on a clean page rather than splitting
       a heading away from its content. */
    section {
      page-break-inside: auto;
    }
    section > h3 {
      page-break-after: avoid;
      break-after: avoid;
    }

    .index-chart {
      margin-bottom: 6pt;
    }

    .footer-note {
      font-size: 8.5pt;
      color: var(--mute);
      border-top: 1pt solid var(--line);
      padding-top: 10pt;
      margin-top: 18pt;
    }

    .disclaimer {
      background: #fef2f2;
      border: 1pt solid #fecaca;
      color: #7f1d1d;
      padding: 10pt 12pt;
      border-radius: 8pt;
      font-size: 9pt;
      margin: 12pt 0;
    }

    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 12pt;
    }

    /* Citizen-summary panel — the "What this means for you" block. The
       tone modifier swaps the accent colour and headline tint so the
       reader's eye lands on the right verdict at a glance. */
    .summary-card {
      border: 1pt solid;
      border-radius: 10pt;
      padding: 14pt 16pt;
      margin: 14pt 0;
      page-break-inside: avoid;
      break-inside: avoid;
    }
    .summary-card.safe { border-color: #bbf7d0; background: #f0fdf4; }
    .summary-card.caution { border-color: #fde68a; background: #fffbeb; }
    .summary-card.avoid { border-color: #fecaca; background: #fef2f2; }
    .summary-card.not_water { border-color: #fde68a; background: #fffbeb; }
    .summary-card.unknown { border-color: var(--line); background: #f8fafc; }
    .summary-pill {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 3pt 8pt;
      border-radius: 999pt;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 8pt;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--paper);
    }
    .summary-pill.safe { background: var(--risk-low); }
    .summary-pill.caution { background: var(--risk-medium); }
    .summary-pill.avoid { background: var(--risk-high); }
    .summary-pill.not_water { background: #92400e; }
    .summary-pill.unknown { background: var(--mute); }
    .summary-headline {
      font-size: 12pt;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin: 6pt 0 4pt;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    .summary-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 10pt;
      margin-top: 10pt;
    }
    .summary-tile {
      border: 1pt solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 6pt;
      padding: 8pt 10pt;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);
      font-size: 9pt;
    }
    .summary-tile-label {
      font-size: 7.5pt;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      color: var(--mute);
      margin: 0 0 4pt;
    }
    .summary-tile-body { margin: 0; line-height: 1.45; }
    .summary-footnote {
      margin-top: 10pt;
      padding: 8pt 10pt;
      border: 1pt solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 6pt;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);
      font-size: 8.5pt;
      color: var(--mute);
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="header">
    <div class="brand">
      {% if brand_logo_data_url %}
        {# Bundled AquaLens brand mark (glyph + wordmark + tagline +
           accent rule) shipped at backend/app/services/templates/
           brand-logo.svg and embedded as a base64 data URL by
           report_generator._load_brand_logo_data_url so WeasyPrint
           doesn't need to resolve any external file paths. #}
        <img class="brand-image" src="{{ brand_logo_data_url }}" alt="AquaLens" />
      {% else %}
        <span class="brand-text">aqualens — analysis report</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="report-title">
      {% if brand_logo_data_url %}<p class="report-kicker-text">Analysis Report</p>{% endif %}
      <h1>{{ location_label }}</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Monitoring window {{ session.start_date }} → {{ session.end_date }}
      </p>
      <p class="meta">
        Generated {{ generated_at }}<br/>
        <span class="session-id">Session {{ session.id }}</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  {% if session.aoi_type and session.aoi_type.value != "water" %}
  <section>
    <div class="aoi-banner aoi-banner-{{ session.aoi_type.value }}">
      <div class="aoi-banner-title">
        {% if session.aoi_type.value == "land" %}This AOI is mostly land
        {% else %}Mixed water and land AOI{% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="aoi-banner-body">
        {% if session.aoi_type.value == "land" %}
          Less than 20% of the polygon passes the open-water test
          (NDWI &gt; 0 <em>and</em> MNDWI &gt; 0). Spectral water-quality
          indices like NDCI and NDTI are <em>not</em> measuring water here —
          they reflect vegetation, soil, or built-up surfaces. Move the AOI
          over an actual water body and re-run before relying on the risk
          score.
        {% else %}
          Only part of the polygon passes the open-water test
          (NDWI &gt; 0 <em>and</em> MNDWI &gt; 0). Water-quality indices over
          the water portion still apply, but land pixels dilute the signal —
          treat the score as approximate.
        {% endif %}
        {% if session.water_fraction is not none %}
          <span class="aoi-banner-fraction">
            · {{ "%.0f" | format(session.water_fraction * 100) }}% water pixels
          </span>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <h3>Risk assessment</h3>
    <div class="risk-card">
      <table class="risk-grid" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true">
        <tr>
          <td class="pill-cell">
            <span class="risk-pill {{ risk.level.value }}">{{ risk.level.value | upper }}</span>
          </td>
          <td class="score-cell">
            <div class="risk-meta">
              <span class="risk-meta-label">Score</span>
              <span class="risk-score">{{ "%.0f" | format(risk.score * 100) }}/100</span>
            </div>
          </td>
          <td class="urgency-cell">
            <div class="risk-meta">
              <span class="risk-meta-label">Urgency</span>
              <span class="risk-meta-value">{{ risk.urgency.value }}</span>
            </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <p style="margin-top: 10pt;"><strong>Recommendation.</strong> {{ risk.recommendation }}</p>
      <p><strong>Reasoning.</strong> {{ risk.reasoning }}</p>
    </div>

    {% if citizen_summary %}
    <div class="summary-card {{ citizen_summary.tone }}">
      <span class="summary-pill {{ citizen_summary.tone }}">
        {% if citizen_summary.tone == "safe" %}Likely safe
        {% elif citizen_summary.tone == "caution" %}Use caution
        {% elif citizen_summary.tone == "avoid" %}Avoid contact
        {% elif citizen_summary.tone == "not_water" %}Not water
        {% else %}Pending{% endif %}
      </span>
      <p class="summary-headline">{{ citizen_summary.headline }}</p>
      <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.5;">{{ citizen_summary.bottom_line }}</p>

      <div class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-tile">
          <p class="summary-tile-label">For you</p>
          <p class="summary-tile-body">{{ citizen_summary.safety_for_humans }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="summary-tile">
          <p class="summary-tile-label">For pets and kids</p>
          <p class="summary-tile-body">{{ citizen_summary.safety_for_pets_and_kids }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="summary-footnote">
        <strong>What we couldn't check.</strong>
        {{ citizen_summary.what_we_could_not_check }}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div style="margin-top: 12pt; border: 1pt solid var(--line); border-radius: 8pt; padding: 10pt 12pt; background: #f8fafc;">
      <p style="margin: 0 0 6pt; font-size: 8.5pt; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--mute);">
        How to read the score
      </p>
      <table style="border: 0; width: 100%;">
        <tr style="border: 0;">
          <td style="border: 0; padding: 2pt 6pt 2pt 0;">
            <span style="display: inline-block; width: 9pt; height: 9pt; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--risk-low); margin-right: 4pt; vertical-align: middle;"></span>
            <strong>Low</strong> · 0–32 · routine cadence is fine
          </td>
          <td style="border: 0; padding: 2pt 6pt;">
            <span style="display: inline-block; width: 9pt; height: 9pt; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--risk-medium); margin-right: 4pt; vertical-align: middle;"></span>
            <strong>Medium</strong> · 33–65 · sample within a week
          </td>
          <td style="border: 0; padding: 2pt 0 2pt 6pt;">
            <span style="display: inline-block; width: 9pt; height: 9pt; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--risk-high); margin-right: 4pt; vertical-align: middle;"></span>
            <strong>High</strong> · 66–100 · sample within 48 hours
          </td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="disclaimer">
      <strong>Advisory only.</strong> AquaLens does not certify water safety,
      detect toxins, or replace laboratory testing. Use these results to
      prioritise field sampling and follow up with accredited methods.
      {{ risk.limitations }}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>Scene metadata</h3>
    <table>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 28%;">Provider</th>
        <td>{{ session.scene_provider or "—" }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Scene ID</th>
        <td>{{ session.scene_id or "—" }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Capture date</th>
        <td>{{ session.scene_capture_date or "—" }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Cloud cover</th>
        <td>{% if session.scene_cloud_cover is not none %}{{ "%.1f" | format(session.scene_cloud_cover) }}%{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Water body area</th>
        <td>{% if water_body.area_km2 %}{{ "%.2f" | format(water_body.area_km2) }} km²{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>Spectral indices</h3>
    <div class="grid">
      {% for idx in indices %}
        <div>
          <div class="index-chart">{{ idx.chart_svg | safe }}</div>
          <div style="font-size: 8.5pt; color: var(--mute);">
            Bands: {{ idx.bands | join(", ") }} · {{ idx.interpretation }}
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if evidence %}
  <section>
    <h3>Field evidence</h3>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Reported</th>
          <th>Color</th>
          <th>Odor</th>
          <th>Algae</th>
          <th>Dead fish</th>
          <th>Rainfall</th>
          <th>Complaints</th>
          <th>Notes</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for ev in evidence %}
        <tr>
          <td>{{ ev.created_at.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M") }}</td>
          <td>{{ ev.water_color.value }}</td>
          <td>{{ ev.odor.value }}</td>
          <td>{{ "yes" if ev.algae_present else "no" }}</td>
          <td>{{ ev.dead_fish_count }}</td>
          <td>{{ "%.1f" | format(ev.rainfall_mm) }} mm</td>
          <td>{{ ev.complaints_count }}</td>
          <td>{{ ev.notes or "" }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if agent_summary and agent_summary.steps %}
  <section>
    <h3>How AquaLens worked this out</h3>
    <p style="margin: 0 0 8pt;">
      This report wasn't written by one model in one go. A small team of
      Gemini agents handled different parts of the job, and the deterministic
      Python core handled the numbers. Here is what each part did for your
      water body, in plain language.
    </p>

    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="width: 22%;">Step</th>
          <th>What it did</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for step in agent_summary.steps %}
        <tr>
          <td>
            <strong>{{ step.label }}</strong><br/>
            <small style="color: var(--mute);">{{ step.subtitle }}</small>
          </td>
          <td>{{ step.body }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    {% if agent_summary.citations %}
    <p class="meta" style="margin-top: 10pt;">
      <strong>External sources the Historian cited</strong>
    </p>
    <ul>
      {% for cite in agent_summary.citations %}
      <li>
        {% if cite.uri %}<a href="{{ cite.uri }}">{{ cite.title or cite.uri }}</a>
        {% else %}{{ cite.title or "(untitled source)" }}{% endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}

    <p class="meta" style="margin-top: 8pt; color: var(--mute);">
      Run details · model {{ agent_summary.gemini_model }} ·
      {{ agent_summary.total_tokens }} tokens ·
      {{ agent_summary.total_latency_ms }} ms total.
    </p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <h3>Glossary</h3>
    <table>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 22%;">NDWI</th>
        <td>Tells us where water actually is — built from near-infrared and short-wave infrared light.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>MNDWI</th>
        <td>Same idea as NDWI but more reliable in cities (uses green light instead of NIR).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>NDTI</th>
        <td>How murky the water looks — a stand-in for suspended sediment.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>NDCI</th>
        <td>A proxy for chlorophyll-a; an early-warning for algal blooms (not a confirmed measurement).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>NDVI</th>
        <td>Vegetation health around the shoreline; stress here often co-occurs with water-quality changes.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>WRI</th>
        <td>A second water-vs-land moisture signal that complements NDWI/MNDWI.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Risk score</th>
        <td>0–100 number combining the indices and any field evidence. Low &lt; 33, Medium &lt; 66, High otherwise.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Urgency</th>
        <td>Routine = next planned visit. Elevated = within a week. Immediate = within 48 hours.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Cloud cover</th>
        <td>Percentage of the satellite scene hidden by clouds. We picked the most recent scene below the threshold you set.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Provider</th>
        <td>Where the imagery came from — Microsoft Planetary Computer's free Sentinel-2 L2A archive.</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </section>

  <footer class="footer-note">
    AquaLens is licensed under the MIT License.
    Sentinel-2 imagery © European Union, contains Copernicus Sentinel data
    accessed via the Microsoft Planetary Computer.
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
